# OSWP Forty Shell — TODO (Big Ticket)

Draft. Review and edit before treating as authoritative.

1. **Markdown/ACF static-page authoring system**
   - Goal: faster authoring, shared authoring (office staff), and
     support for pages that are edited often (e.g. sponsor lists) —
     without building a full CMS/schema solution.
   - Design agreed: one ACF field ("Page Content — Markdown") + one
     reusable WP Page Template (not a `page-{slug}.php` per page) +
     Parsedown (vendored, not a plugin) to render it.
   - New page creation stays CLI/maintainer-only. Editing existing
     pages moves to the WP GUI for whoever has the role.
   - Needs: a `content-editor` WP role — edit existing pages, cannot
     create/publish/delete. WordPress doesn't cleanly separate
     "edit" from "create" by capability alone, so this needs a
     small custom capability + hidden "Add New" button. Not
     watertight against a determined user, but sufficient for normal
     office use.
   - Not yet built. No code written.

2. **Footer: link structure**
   - Likely intent: separate static pages into footer-menu groupings
     rather than one flat list. Started as "four dummy links," real
     shape depends on item 3 (site map).
   - Not yet built. No structure decided yet.

3. **Site map**
   - Needed before template decisions can be finalised. Only two
     templates are locked in so far: billboard (`page-billboard.php`,
     mechanism proven) and plain single page (`page-ipsum.php`
     pattern, via `oswp_forty_start()`/`oswp_forty_end()`).
   - This also decides the fate of the remaining Twenty
     Twenty-Five–shell pages (`next7days`, `recurring`,
     `events-schema`, `single-event`) — which stay and get migrated
     to Forty vs which get deleted. CSS cleanup and PHP migration for
     those pages both follow from that decision, so don't action
     either separately until the site map settles it.

4. **VPS staging deployment**
   - Get a working copy live on the VPS so stakeholders can see dev
     progress in real time, rather than reviewing screenshots/
     localhost only.
   - Not yet started. Will need the standard domain-swap step
     (`siteurl`/`home` options, permalink flush) once a URL/subdomain
     is chosen — flagged as straightforward in earlier discussion,
     not yet executed.
